# My app

Started from the Stack Junkie Style showcase with the {{presetLabel}} preset.

Requires a C++17 compiler, CMake 3.21 or later, and Qt 6.4 or later with Widgets and Svg, discoverable through `CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH`.

```sh
cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
cmake --build build --config Release
```

- CMake uses an installed Stack Junkie Style package when `CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH` finds one. Otherwise it fetches the `{{tag}}` release tag of {{repository}}.
- `main.cpp` holds the preset and the choices changed from it.
- `main.cpp` opens with two areas of three pages each. Their names and content are Stubs: a Debug build shows them striped, and a Release build fails at each one until it is replaced.
- On Windows, run `windeployqt` on the built program to copy the Qt runtime beside it.
